<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kochi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cochin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kochi, historically Cochin, is a port city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malabar-coast">Malabar Coast</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It rose as a harbour after a flood of 1341 opened its natural channel and became capital of the Kingdom of Cochin. The Portuguese built their first fort in India there in 1503, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> took it in 1663. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a> died there in 1524, and Fort Kochi keeps old churches and a synagogue.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kochi.jpg" alt="Kochi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fsquares (The Ibrahims) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kochi_Skyline.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
